  "text": "I authorize implementation under the frozen G-ROUTE4 design step 4.\n\nProceed from the closed external corpus review round 1 at commit \"30b488a3434f69ffb1edb9b46533e4ecc1e19eba\".\n\nTreat the reviewed 26-fix corpus, its gold, the round-1 closure, the adjudication records, the successor reports, the frozen blueprint and the seal as authoritative inputs.\n\nImplementation must remain subordinate to the frozen design. Do not change the reviewed corpus, gold, thresholds, success criteria, adjudication outcomes, review findings, independence definitions or frozen methodology merely to make implementation pass.\n\nImplement the step-4 infrastructure required by the frozen design, including \"g_route4_independence\" and its deterministic checks, with explicit provenance back to the reviewed/frozen inputs.\n\nPreserve these boundaries:\n\n- do not move or rewrite \"main\", \"g-route4/seal\", or \"g-route4-seal\";\n- do not modify sealed or historical review artifacts;\n- do not reinterpret completed adjudication;\n- do not weaken any frozen threshold or qualification condition;\n- do not begin live/model campaign execution unless the frozen design explicitly makes it part of this implementation stage and all implementation prerequisites have passed;\n- preserve failure artifacts and stop at any boundary requiring operator disposition.\n\nB7 is mandatory during this stage:\n\nAfter \"g_route4_independence\" is implemented, run the required final pre-freeze independence re-check with that forked module against the reviewed 26-fix corpus.\n\nIt must reproduce the frozen values and satisfy the same bounds.\n\nThe earlier pinned-tool reproduction does not waive or substitute for B7. If the forked-module result differs materially, violates a bound, or cannot reproduce the required frozen values, stop and preserve the failure rather than changing the criterion.\n\nAlso carry B8 into the eventual freeze records by binding the B′ fix-round per-cell counts already preserved in the closure addendum.\n\nBefore any freeze decision, run the deterministic implementation checks required by the frozen design and verify that the implementation has not altered the reviewed inputs or historical records.\n\nProceed with implementation now. Do not freeze or begin the next campaign merely because implementation completes; stop at the next operator-decision boundary defined by the frozen procedure."
 },
